## 4. Zero-Allocation Streaming Architecture

### 4.1 In-Place Decryption Topology
High-throughput telemetry processing requires parsing gigabyte-scale flight logs with zero GC pressure and zero heap allocations.

```text
Log Buffer: [ ... | Type | Len | Seed | Encrypted Ciphertext ... | 0xFF | ... ]
                     │      │     │                 │
                     │      │     └─────────┬───────┘
                     ▼      ▼               ▼
      RawRecordEnvelope<'a>             [XOR Keystream]
               │                                │
               │   out_buf: [ ... scratch buffer (e.g. 1024 B on stack) ... ]
               │                 │
               │                 ▼
               │      Step 1: Write XOR-descrambled Ciphertext into out_buf
               │                 │
               │                 ▼
               │      Step 2: Read next_iv = out_buf[len - 16 .. len]
               │                 │
               │                 ▼
               │      Step 3: AES-256-CBC Decrypt in-place inside out_buf
               │                 │
               │                 ▼
               │      Step 4: PKCS7 Unpad in-place (adjust slice boundary)
               │                 │
               │                 ▼
               │      Step 5: ivs[fp] = next_iv
               │                 │
               ▼                 ▼
        Telemetry Record Parser (e.g. OsdRecord::parse(plaintext_slice))
```

### 4.2 Stack-Allocated Caller Example
```rust
let header = TxtHeader::parse(&file_bytes)?;
let mut iter = RecordEnvelopeIterator::new(&file_bytes, &header)?
    .with_key(1, base_key, base_iv)
    .with_key(10, gimbal_key, gimbal_iv);

// Fixed 1KB scratch buffer reused across millions of iterations
let mut scratch = [0u8; 1024];

while let Some(env_res) = iter.next() {
    let env = env_res?;
    let plaintext = iter.decode_into(&env, &mut scratch)?;

    match env.record_type {
        1 => {
            let osd = OsdRecord::parse(plaintext)?;
            // Process telemetry with ZERO allocations
        }
        3 => {
            let gimbal = GimbalRecord::parse(plaintext)?;
        }
        _ => {}
    }
}
```

